hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15597","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from a mawla of theirs, Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Usayd, from a man of Khuzaah called Muharrish or Mukharrish, Sufyan did not confirm his name, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from al-Jiranah by night and performed Umrah, then returned and morning came as one spending the night there. I looked at his back as an ingot of silver."
